// A Sin That Defines You (D10), p.18-19.
(
    name: "Sin",
    die: D10,
    entries: [
        (1, 1, (title: "Pride", text: "You refuse to kneel. The Choir demands subservience and the Flesh demands dissolution, but your ego is a fortress of iron. You are too significant, too yourself, to be reshaped into a mindless instrument or ground into meaningless pulp. In the face of gods, your arrogance is your shield.")),
        (2, 2, (title: "Wrath", text: "The apocalypse is not a cosmic event, it's a personal insult. The Choir or the Flesh took something from you (a home, a loved one, your future), and now a burning, all-consuming hatred is all you have left. This vengeful fire purifies you of their influence, leaving no room for faith or fear. You will not break until you have answered their atrocities in kind.")),
        (3, 3, (title: "Heresy", text: "You spit on their apocalypse. The Choir is not divine and the Flesh is not primordial; they are abominations, cosmic mistakes to be defied. Your anchor is a blasphemous counter-faith: a belief in a forgotten god, a pact with a devil, or a self-made philosophy that declares both powers to be liars. Your conviction in a different truth makes you immune to theirs. Or so you hope.")),
        (4, 4, (title: "Avarice", text: "Gold is real. A sword is real. A full belly is real. You cling to the tangible, material world with a ferocious greed. The Choir's promises are just noise and the Flesh's hunger is a problem for others. While zealots and monsters war over the nature of reality, you are grounded by what you can hold, count, and own.")),
        (5, 5, (title: "Deceit", text: "Your entire identity is a lie, a carefully constructed falsehood so profound that sometimes you even believe it yourself. You are a runaway noble posing as a peasant, a charlatan who feigns piety, a coward who wears the mask of a hero. The Choir cannot remake a soul that isn't real, and the Flesh cannot unmake a phantom. Your lie is your armor.")),
        (6, 6, (title: "Despair", text: "You have seen the truth, and it is empty. There is no salvation, no grand design, no final reward. The Choir's song is a lie and the Flesh's silence is oblivion. This profound hopelessness is your liberation. With nothing to hope for and nothing left to lose, you cannot be tempted by promises of rapture or terrified by the threat of dissolution.")),
        (7, 7, (title: "Obsession", text: "The world may be ending, but you have a task to complete. You are fixated on a singular, earthly goal: to deliver a letter, to find a lost tome, to kill a specific man, to taste wine from a certain vintage one last time. This fixation narrows your world to a single point, rendering the cosmic war an irrelevant distraction. Your focus is absolute, and it leaves no room for their influence.")),
        (8, 8, (title: "Gluttony", text: "You are defined by a ravenous hunger for life. Not just for food, but for sensation, for experience, for the visceral, messy reality of being alive. You refuse to be consumed by the Flesh because you yourself are too busy consuming, and you reject the Choir's sterile harmony for the chaotic symphony of earthly pleasure and pain. Your insatiable appetite for life itself is a defiant roar in the face of the end.")),
        (9, 9, (title: "Apathy", text: "You simply do not care. The sky bleeds song, the earth writhes into meat… it is loud, unpleasant, and ultimately, not your problem. This profound emotional detachment insulates you from the Choir's ecstasy and the Flesh's terror. It is not a conscious choice but a fundamental state of being. The end of the world is happening to other people.")),
        (10, 10, (title: "Doubt", text: "You believe in nothing. Every miracle is a trick, every prayer is wasted breath, every horror a natural phenomenon not yet understood. You question everything and everyone, from the pronouncements of a singing angel to the tremors of the flesh-eaten ground. Your anchor is a deep, unshakeable skepticism that corrodes faith and fear alike. You cannot be converted if you refuse to believe.")),
    ],
)
